# zig fmt canonicalises to LF. Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF and
# `zig fmt --check` reports every file in the repo as unformatted, which buries
# the ones that genuinely are.
*.zig text eol=lf
*.zon text eol=lf

# Same reason, for the text `core.autocrlf=true` was still converting. Without
# these, a file's worktree bytes differ from its committed blob while `git diff`
# normalises the difference away and reports nothing — so a tool that hashes or
# byte-compares a file disagrees with version control and cannot be told why.
# That cost real time twice: `tools/mutate.py` restored source as CRLF and made
# `cmd_job.zig`'s adjacency gate fail with `FunctionUnterminated` for mutations
# in unrelated files, and the byte sizes quoted for the evidence artefacts were
# measured on CRLF worktree copies and so overstated the committed blobs.
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
